-- 0103_entity_prose_house_style.sql
--
-- House style and canon for the seeded profile prose that lives only in the
-- database (issue #704). Two changes to entities.meta, in one statement:
--
-- 1. No em dashes. 181 profiles (club, stadium, training facility, manager,
--    staff, player, referee, journalist, pundit, media company) carried an em
--    dash in 221 prose fields. Each sentence was rewritten by hand with a
--    colon, comma, parentheses or a new sentence, the same judgment as #702.
--    No other words change. content/profiles/*.json (the seed source) carries
--    the identical rewrites, so a reseed cannot bring the dashes back.
--
-- 2. Canon. The 32 club profiles lose profile.trophy_cabinet and
--    profile.legends: both predate and contradict the canon register
--    (src/data/lore.generated.ts), which owns honours and legends. #703
--    stopped rendering them and nothing else reads them. Jupiter Titans'
--    "Most trophies of any outer-system club" (false: Ceres Miners have 73
--    against Jupiter's 72) becomes "Most league titles in Gas/Ice Giants League history"
--    (38, ahead of Europa Oceanic's 33).
--
-- ORDER: apply only after the code that makes trophy_cabinet and legends
-- optional in teamProfileSchema is deployed. The old schema requires them,
-- so the club pages would drop the whole profile.
--
-- GUARDED AND IDEMPOTENT: each row carries the md5 of its meta::text as read
-- from production on 2026-11-26. A row is replaced only while its meta still
-- equals that snapshot, so a row edited since is skipped (and reported),
-- and a second run updates nothing. The whole meta is replaced, which is
-- safe for exactly that reason.
--
-- VERIFY after applying: scripts/sql/verify-0103-entity-prose.sql (read only)
-- must return fingerprint 633e63a2e0c5702b674077815d1010dd for these 181 rows.
--
-- Generated from the production snapshot; do not edit by hand.

